  "notes": "{絶望|ぜつぼう} is a powerful word expressing complete loss of hope—utter despair.\n\nFORMS:\n{絶|ぜつ} (to cut off) + {望|ぼう} (hope) = hope cut off\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {絶望|ぜつぼう}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to despair\n- {絶望|ぜつぼう}⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{陥|おちい}る→陥る：14537_ochiiru⟧: to fall into despair\n- {絶望|ぜつぼう}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{淵|ふち}→淵：13456_fuchi⟧: the depths of despair\n- ⟦{絶望的|ぜつぼうてき}→絶望的：15404_zetsubouteki⟧⟦な→な：09497_na⟧⟦{状況|じょうきょう}→状況：01576_joukyou⟧: hopeless situation\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {絶望|ぜつぼう}: despair, hopelessness\n- ⟦{希望|きぼう}→希望：00221_kibou⟧: hope (antonym)\n- ⟦{失望|しつぼう}→失望：03183_shitsubou⟧: disappointment (less severe)\n\nUSAGE:\n{絶望|ぜつぼう} is stronger than ⟦{失望|しつぼう}→失望：03183_shitsubou⟧ (disappointment). It implies a complete, devastating loss of all hope.",
